    {
      "name": "mus_morning2",
      "type": "music",
      "text": "Funny, bouncy Chinese folk comedy theme for a cheeky cooking vlog starring a jolly, greedy old poet: staccato plucked pipa and guzheng play a mischievous tiptoeing melody, a plucked zhongruan bass bounces on the off-beats, comic woodblock and temple-block hits, playful pitch bends and little slides like a wink, now and then a short squeaky suona note as a punchline, G major pentatonic, 120 bpm, witty, sunny and light, it starts at once with the plucked melody. Instrumental, no vocals.",
      "model": null,
      "status": 200,
      "sfx": true,
      "file": "mus_morning2.mp3",
      "bytes": 1490277,
      "seconds": 62.19
    },
    {
      "name": "mus_huangzhou2",
      "type": "music",
      "text": "A mock-grand, tongue-in-cheek flashback: a pompous, overly serious bamboo flute (dizi) melody over a slow gong roll, answered by a cheeky plucked pipa phrase, nostalgic and funny, an old man bragging about the pork he invented, D major pentatonic, 76 bpm. Instrumental, no vocals.",
      "model": null,
      "status": 200,
      "sfx": true,
      "file": "mus_huangzhou2.mp3",
      "bytes": 337337,
      "seconds": 14.08
    },
    {
      "name": "mus_noon2",
      "type": "music",
      "text": "Lazy comic nap music: a sleepy, sliding erhu yawns over tiptoeing pizzicato guzheng plucks, a sly little melody that keeps nearly dozing off, woodblock ticks like a clock, cheeky and drowsy, a funny old man stuffing himself with lychees in the shade, G major pentatonic, 84 bpm. Instrumental, no vocals.",
      "model": null,
      "status": 200,
      "sfx": true,
      "file": "mus_noon2.mp3",
